WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.769
[music playing]

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.742
At that point in
time, my main mission,

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.510
get it back to Australia.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.848
We bought a whole
heap of crystal meth

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:20.286
from Zack's suppliers, big
SnapLock bags of drugs.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:22.522
And we bought a whole
heap of gift sets

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:23.923
that had bath salts in them.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:29.863
There was a process.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:34.534
We would have to make sure that
we had gloves on, hairnets.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.406
Then we'd lay out
plastic because we

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:43.676
didn't want any kind of evidence
left, no fingerprints, no DNA.

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:47.947
And we were naked.

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.685
It's like open heart surgery.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:56.189
Take the soap out,
separate it all.

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.490
With screw jars,
they have, like,

00:00:57.557 --> 00:01:00.927
the plastic around the side.

00:01:00.994 --> 00:01:03.763
I would cut that plastic,
empty the contents,

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:08.268
like, into a bowl, weigh
it, making sure that match

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:11.438
the weight of it on the jar.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:15.642
I don't want any residue
on the outside of the jar.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:18.311
I would get a very
fine blowtorch

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:24.350
and I'd seal it, put all
the stuff back into the box.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.620
It looks as about as
not tampered with as I

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.189
could possibly make it.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:41.668
Once the product was perfect,
it got shipped with other items

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.735
that had to go out.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.904
So it all looked part
of the same parcel

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.407
with my company
name on the back.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:48.441
See ya.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.285
These packages
would get tracked.

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:01.054
Once we knew it got
there a few days later,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.022
we were heaps excited about it.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.457
Then the money would be wired.

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:09.529
The job was done.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:12.098
We started sending packages
on a regular basis.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:17.337
It worked out to be
about $320,000 a month.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.472
It wasn't going to be
forever, and then I

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:23.376
could legitimize myself
and focus on my modeling.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:29.916
I'd be in front of the camera,
boom, in my mind, I'm like, oh,

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:33.019
got to get a gift set today
that had bath salts in them.

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:35.188
And that's what I'm
thinking as I'm getting

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.123
told to pull my midsection in.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.925
I lived a double life.

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:43.463
By day, I'm a swimsuit model
gracing the pages of magazines,

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:48.234
nighttime I'm packaging
drugs to send overseas.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:54.274
Those two worlds for
me were very real

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.376
and I couldn't
have them collide.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:05.652
I now had so much
money, it's obscene.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.087
I could just walk into
anywhere, purchase

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:10.957
whatever I wanted
at whatever time,

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.659
and not even blink an eyelid.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.198
I walked around
thinking I was the best

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:22.702
thing since sliced bread.

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.103
What are you doing today?

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.873
We're going to go and watch a
show in Broadway in New York.

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:28.341
I'm going to book a flight now.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:29.275
Can't get a flight?

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.410
Let's get a G6.

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:36.549
It's-- yeah.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:42.188
I wish in my mind now that
I looked at those times

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:43.856
and thought, that
could send me to jail

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.091
for the rest of my life.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.293
But I didn't know any different.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:53.766
When you have financial
freedom like that,

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:58.071
if you have no
discipline, you run amok.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:01.774
And that's pretty
much what happened.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:06.646
I wasn't turning up for
shoots, drugs were rife.

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:10.550
It wasn't a cause of my demise,
but we got out of control.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:16.189
I thought, the power, the
success, and the money,

00:04:16.255 --> 00:04:18.691
and I would be happy
for once in my life.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:19.659
And I wasn't.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:25.999
I was not fulfilled.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.101
I had not found love.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.169
I was so hollow and empty.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.242
Why can't I just go
into the supermarket

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:39.812
and then there'd be,
like, a can of, like, love

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.781
and a can of family,
and I'll buy all that

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:45.551
and I'll be right, because
I knew what was missing,

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:46.486
you know.

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:50.256
[music playing]

